cff-version: 1.2.0
title: open-king
message: >-
  open-king is an independent, clean-room reimplementation. If you use
  relatedness inference in published research, cite the original KING
  paper (Manichaikul et al. 2010) — listed below under
  `references` — and, if it is useful to say which implementation
  produced your numbers, this software as well.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gu
    given-names: Wanjun
repository-code: https://github.com/Broccolito/open-king
abstract: >-
  A clean-room, MIT-licensed Rust reimplementation of KING
  (Kinship-based INference for Genome-wide association studies),
  targeting byte-identical output with the reference KING 2.3.2 binary
  on PLINK 1 filesets. Written from the published algorithms, the
  public documentation and black-box observation of the reference
  binary; no KING source code was read or copied.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - kinship
  - relatedness
  - IBD segments
  - GWAS quality control
  - PLINK

references:
  # The method open-king implements. Cite this for the estimators.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Robust relationship inference in genome-wide association studies
    authors:
      - family-names: Manichaikul
        given-names: Ani
      - family-names: Mychaleckyj
        given-names: Josyf C.
      - family-names: Rich
        given-names: Stephen S.
      - family-names: Daly
        given-names: Kathy
      - family-names: Sale
        given-names: Michèle
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Wei-Min
    journal: Bioinformatics
    year: 2010
    volume: 26
    issue: 22
    start: 2867
    end: 2873
    doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btq559

  # The original program. open-king is not affiliated with it, not endorsed
  # by it, and not derived from its source; it is credited here because it
  # is the work this project reimplements and measures itself against.
  - type: software
    title: KING — Kinship-based INference for Genome-wide association studies
    authors:
      - family-names: Chen
        given-names: Wei-Min
    version: 2.3.2
    year: 2023
    url: https://www.kingrelatedness.com/
    notes: >-
      The reference implementation, by Wei-Min Chen and colleagues at the
      University of Virginia. It remains the work of its authors under its
      own license terms. open-king reproduces its observable behaviour;
      it contains none of its code.
